\subsection{E.2 Mathematical Formalization and Residual Convergence}

Scientific certainty is quantified through convergence metrics. Deterministic
predictability requires:
\begin{equation}
\phi^{(k+1)} = \phi^{(k)} + \Delta t\,\mathcal{R}[\phi^{(k)}],
\end{equation}
with reproducibility under identical initial conditions.

Uncertainty quantification (UQ) bounds variance:
\begin{equation}
\sigma_{\text{UQ}}^2 = \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^N
\left(\phi_i - \bar{\phi}\right)^2,
\end{equation}
ensuring that stochastic fluctuations do not alter core conclusions.

